    points: ['Flats and small L37 cottages', 'About 4 to 5 hours', 'Cleaner, inhibitor and report included'] },
  { id: 'standard', tier: '3-bed homes', name: '7 to 10 radiators', price: '£525', unit: 'fixed price, inc VAT',
    points: ['3-bed semis and bungalows', 'About 5 to 7 hours', 'Cleaner, inhibitor and report included'] },
  { id: 'large', tier: 'Most Formby homes', popular: true, name: '11 to 15 radiators', price: '£675', unit: 'fixed price, inc VAT',
    points: ['4 and 5-bed homes in Formby and Freshfield', 'About 7 to 9 hours', 'Each zone flushed in turn'] },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is a powerflush the same as power flushing?', a: 'Yes. Powerflush, power flush and powerflushing all mean the same job. A pump pushes cleaning chemicals through your radiators and boiler to clear sludge. In Formby ours costs £395 for up to 6 radiators.' },
  { q: 'How much does power flushing cost in Formby?', a: 'It is £395 for up to 6 radiators, £525 for 7 to 10 and £675 for 11 to 15. Each radiator over 15 is £40. All prices include VAT. Cleaner, inhibitor and a written report are included.' },
  { q: 'My Formby house has 18 radiators. What will it cost?', a: 'It is £675 for the first 15, plus £40 for each one over that. So 18 radiators is £795 including VAT. We give you the fixed price on the phone.' },
  { q: 'Do you cover all L37 postcodes?', a: 'Yes. We cover all of Formby and Freshfield, plus Hightown, Ainsdale, Crosby and Maghull. The price is the same everywhere, with no travel charge.' },
  { q: 'Can you flush a system with more than one heating zone?', a: 'Yes. Many Formby homes have separate zones for upstairs and downstairs. We flush one zone at a time, with the other zones shut off. That way each zone gets the full flow of the machine.' },
  { q: 'Do you flush underfloor heating loops?', a: 'Yes, where they are part of the same system. We flush each loop on its own through the manifold. If only the underfloor is cold and the radiators are fine, the fault may be the manifold pump. We check that first.' },
  { q: 'Will a flush help my boiler warranty?', a: 'Boiler makers need the system cleaned and treated to BS 7593. Our written report shows when the system was cleaned and what inhibitor went in. Keep it with your boiler papers.' },
  { q: 'My boiler was fitted without a flush. Is it too late?', a: 'No. A flush now clears the old sludge before it does more harm to the new heat exchanger. The written report also gives you a record for your boiler papers.' },
  { q: 'How long does a power flush take in a large house?', a: 'Usually one day. A 4-bed home with 10 to 14 radiators takes 7 to 9 hours. A big multi-zone house with underfloor loops can take a full day.' },
  { q: 'Can a power flush cause leaks?', a: 'It can show up a weak spot that was already there, like a radiator rusted almost through. We check radiators and joints first. If a part fails on the day, we price the fix before we do it.' },
  { q: 'Do I need to be home?', a: 'Someone needs to let us in and be there at the end, when we show you every zone working. The heating and hot water are off for part of the day.' },
];
---

