  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="prices-detail">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How much does power flushing cost in Formby?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A power flush in Formby costs £395 for up to 6 radiators, £525 for 7 to 10 and £675 for 11 to 15. All prices include VAT.</p>
      <p>Most 4 and 5-bed Formby homes have 11 to 15 radiators, so £675 is our most common price here. Count every radiator, including towel rails. There is no extra charge for zones.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table stk">
          <thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Price inc VAT</th><th>Typical Formby home</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>Power flush, up to 6 radiators</strong></td><td data-label="Price inc VAT">£395</td><td data-label="Typical Formby home">Flats and small cottages in Formby village</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>Power flush, 7 to 10 radiators</strong></td><td data-label="Price inc VAT">£525</td><td data-label="Typical Formby home">3-bed semis and bungalows</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>Power flush, 11 to 15 radiators</strong></td><td data-label="Price inc VAT">£675</td><td data-label="Typical Formby home">4 and 5-bed homes in Formby and Freshfield</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>Each radiator over 15</strong></td><td data-label="Price inc VAT">+£40</td><td data-label="Typical Formby home">Large detached homes</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>Chemical system clean</strong></td><td data-label="Price inc VAT">£195</td><td data-label="Typical Formby home">Newer systems with mild signs</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>Single radiator flush</strong></td><td data-label="Price inc VAT">£95</td><td data-label="Typical Formby home">One cold radiator, rest of the system fine</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>Magnetic filter fitted</strong></td><td data-label="Price inc VAT">£150 with a flush, £195 alone</td><td data-label="Typical Formby home">Keeping the system clean after</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Job"><strong>Power flush with a new boiler</strong></td><td data-label="Price inc VAT">£350</td><td data-label="Typical Formby home">Fitted on the same job as a <a href="/boiler-installation-formby">new boiler</a></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>What is included</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>A water test before we start and after we finish</li>
        <li>A machine flush of every radiator, one at a time</li>
        <li>Each heating zone flushed in turn</li>
        <li>A full dose of corrosion inhibitor to BS 7593</li>
        <li>Radiators balanced and the pressure set</li>
        <li>A written report to keep with your boiler papers</li>
      </ul>
      <p>There is no call-out fee and no travel charge. If only one radiator is cold, we will say so. A £95 single radiator flush may be all you need.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="larger">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Why is power flushing different in larger Formby homes?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Formby homes tend to be bigger, with more radiators and often more than one heating zone. Each zone needs its own flush to get a full result.</p>
      <h3>More radiators, more sludge</h3>
      <p>A typical 4-bed detached house in Formby has 12 to 15 radiators. That is a lot of steel slowly rusting inside. Big rooms often have big radiators, and they tend to show cold spots first.</p>
      <h3>Zones flushed one at a time</h3>
      <p>Many Formby homes have separate zones for upstairs and downstairs. Flush them all at once and each zone gets only part of the flow. So we open one zone at a time and close the rest. Then we flush each radiator in that zone on its own.</p>
      <h3>Underfloor loops</h3>
      <p>Kitchen extensions here often have underfloor heating on the same system. We flush each loop on its own through the manifold. It adds time, but every part of the system gets cleaned.</p>
      <h3>System boilers and cylinders</h3>
      <p>Many larger homes run a system boiler with a hot water cylinder. Our engineers are all G3 qualified for unvented cylinders. If your cylinder needs work too, see our <a href="/hot-water-cylinders-formby">Formby cylinder page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="signs">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Does my Formby heating need a power flush?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">The clearest sign is a radiator that is warm at the top and cold at the bottom. If you spot two of the signs below, it is worth a check.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Big radiators cold at the bottom.</strong> Sludge sinks to the base. Bleeding will not fix it.</li>
        <li><strong>One zone heats much slower than the other.</strong> The slow zone likely has more sludge blocking the flow.</li>
        <li><strong>Black water when you bleed a radiator.</strong> That is iron oxide sludge, and it is going through your boiler.</li>
        <li><strong>The house takes far longer to warm up.</strong> On a big system, this costs more gas each winter.</li>
        <li><strong>A kettling or banging boiler.</strong> Often sludge from an old system that was not flushed when the boiler was fitted.</li>
        <li><strong>Your boiler went onto old radiators with no flush.</strong> Old sludge may already be in the new heat exchanger.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>When a flush will not help:</strong> it will not fix a failed zone valve, a broken pump or a failed boiler part. If your boiler keeps losing pressure, that is a leak, and it needs finding first. We check this before we suggest a flush.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="how">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How long does a Formby power flush take?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Most Formby homes take one day. We start in the morning and do not leave until every zone and radiator is working.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Home</th><th>Typical time</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Small L37 cottage or 3-bed home, one zone, up to 8 radiators</td><td>4 to 6 hours</td></tr>
            <tr><td>4-bed home, one or two zones, 10 to 14 radiators</td><td>7 to 9 hours</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Large Freshfield detached, several zones and underfloor loops</td><td>A full day</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>What happens on the day</h3>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Check and test (20 to 30 minutes).</strong> We map the zones and any underfloor loops. We check for weak spots and test the water.</li>
        <li><strong>Add the cleaner.</strong> Fernox F3 for a standard clean, or Sentinel X400 for heavy sludge. It runs through every zone first.</li>
        <li><strong>Connect the machine (30 minutes).</strong> Our Kamco CF90 Quantum2 pump goes on at the heating pump or across a radiator.</li>
        <li><strong>Flush zone by zone (most of the day).</strong> One zone at a time, then each radiator in it on its own, with the flow reversed.</li>
        <li><strong>Flush until clear.</strong> We run until the water comes back clean, then test it again.</li>
        <li><strong>Inhibitor, balance and report (30 minutes).</strong> We add inhibitor to BS 7593, balance every zone and give you a written report.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Know how many radiators you have?</strong> Call and we will give you a fixed Formby price on the phone.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="right">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Is a power flush right for my Formby home?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">If your system is over 10 years old with cold radiators or black water, usually yes. If it is newer with mild signs, a £195 chemical clean may do.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>A flush is a good fit if</h3>
          <ul class="brx-list">
            <li>You have cold spots, slow warm-up or a noisy boiler</li>
            <li>One zone heats worse than the other</li>
            <li>Your boiler was fitted to old radiators with no flush</li>
            <li>You are about to fit a new boiler</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Talk to us first if</h3>
          <ul class="brx-list">
            <li>Your boiler keeps losing pressure (that is a leak)</li>
            <li>Only the underfloor is cold, not the radiators</li>
            <li>A zone will not come on at all</li>
            <li>Only one radiator is cold</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>If a zone will not come on, the zone valve may have failed. A flush will not fix that, but we can find it and price a new one. If a radiator is past saving, see our <a href="/radiators-formby">Formby radiator prices</a>, from £245 supplied and fitted.</p>
      <p>We will tell you which job you need, not sell you the bigger one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="warranty">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Does a power flush protect my boiler warranty?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">It helps. Boiler makers need the system cleaned and treated to BS 7593, or they can refuse a warranty claim. Our written report is your record that it was done.</p>
      <p>Many Formby homes have fairly new boilers with long maker warranties. If sludge damages the heat exchanger, the maker may blame the dirty system. The report shows the date, the cleaner used and the inhibitor dose. Keep it with your boiler papers.</p>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>Getting a new boiler from us?</strong> We check the system on every <a href="/boiler-installation-formby">Formby boiler installation</a>. If it needs a flush, it is £350 on the same job.</p></div>
      <h3>Keeping it clean after</h3>
      <p>Fit a magnetic filter to catch new sludge. It is £150 with a flush. Then have the inhibitor checked at your yearly <a href="/boiler-service-formby">boiler service</a>. A clean system can go many years without another flush.</p>
      <h3>Who does the work?</h3>
      <p>Our power flushes are done by our Gas Safe registered engineers, part of our team led by James. You can check any engineer on the <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk/">Gas Safe Register</a>. Every job has a 12-month workmanship guarantee and £2 million public liability insurance.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
